# File: tests/unit/test_ue_compile_gate.py
# Generated from: specs/202-build-the-ue-compile-gate-without-uba-so-parallel-worktrees-don-t-corrupt-each-other-s-objects/requirements.md
Feature: gate-ue-compile builds each checkout without UBA

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: The gate passes -NoUBA to Build.sh
    Given a fake Build.sh under a temporary UE_ROOT that logs its arguments
    And a placeholder dogfood .uproject
    When the project.ue-compile provider runs the engine build for target "DogfoodEditor"
    Then Build.sh receives "DogfoodEditor", "Mac", "Development", "-Project=<absolute project path>", "-WaitMutex" and "-NoUBA"
    And the provider returns "passed" with "-NoUBA" in its recorded command

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The documented gate command shows -NoUBA and why
    Given steering/snippets/project-tech.md
    When a contributor reads the gate-ue-compile row of the Verification Gates table
    Then the row shows the Build.sh command with "-NoUBA"
    And it says the flag turns off the Unreal Build Accelerator
